IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 7114 of 2021
CITATION: (2010) 3 SCC 480
YEAR: 2010

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Dalveer Bhandari, H.S. Bedi

PARTIES:
Kusum Sharma vs Batra Hospital

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Consumer Protection Act, 1986

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 14 Consumer Protection

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
principles of medical negligence, error of judgment vs negligence, medical practitioner safeguards

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Laid down comprehensive 11-point guidelines distinguishing between a bonafide clinical error of judgment and actionable medical negligence.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 14 Consumer Protection.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

